    "120758171": {
      "title": "Some relations between nonexpansive and order preserving mappings",
      "abstract": "Abstract : It is shown that nonlinear operators which preserve the integral are order preserving if and only if they are nonexpansive in L(1) and that those wich commute with translation by a constant are order preserving if and only if they are nonexpansive in L(infinity). Examples are presented and involving partial differential equations, difference approximations and rearrangements. (Author)"
